{"post_stream":{"posts":[{"id":484170,"name":"Danny","username":"DannyB","avatar_template":"/user_avatar/forum.cursor.com/dannyb/{size}/119004_2.png","created_at":"2026-09-05T18:06:12.508Z","cooked":"\u003cp\u003eWhat is the best way to go about exporting/backing up each bot’s individual memory, as well as the shared bot memory?\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eI’m not referring to backing up chats, I’m not interested in those.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eI’m looking to export all of the persistent data, or as Dean Rie put it on another thread:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cblockquote\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe bot’s durable state (profile, memory, routines, skills, connectors, files on the shared computer)\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003c/blockquote\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eI don’t have any custom skills whatsoever currently, AFAIK.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eI thought about having each bot create a \u003ccode\u003eskill.md\u003c/code\u003e file for each topic in its individual memory, and having the Chief of Staff create a \u003ccode\u003eskill.md\u003c/code\u003e file for each topic in the shared memory.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eI saw that it is possible to transfer a certain topic from one bot’s individual memory to another bot’s individual memory. I have done this when I created a new bot for a niche purpose. I had another bot doing that niche work before. When I made the new bot, I watched as it “transferred” about 55 memories on that niche topic to the new bot; erasing them from its own individual memory as it went along.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eSo it looks like it is certainly possible to ascertain which memories relate to each topic, so I guess it is possible to make \u003ccode\u003eskill.md\u003c/code\u003e files for each topic?\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eI cannot say enough how much I absolutely love Grok Bot! It is hands-down the best piece of tech that I’ve ever used! (Using Lauren’s pstack). However the pricing currently makes it impossible to use (1 week’s usage lasts me 8 hours).\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eI’m considering trying/switching to Hermes (despite its flaws that I’ve heard about), so I’m going to do this export from Grok Bot on my last week (currently 2 weeks in to a 1 month Cursor Ultra subscription).\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThanks a lot guys!\u003c/p\u003e","post_number":1,"post_type":1,"posts_count":5,"updated_at":"2026-09-10T18:32:25.810Z","reply_count":0,"reply_to_post_number":null,"quote_count":0,"incoming_link_count":13,"reads":13,"readers_count":12,"score":67.6,"yours":false,"topic_id":170714,"topic_slug":"best-way-to-export-memory","display_username":"Danny","primary_group_name":null,"flair_name":null,"flair_url":null,"flair_bg_color":null,"flair_color":null,"flair_group_id":null,"badges_granted":[],"version":9,"can_edit":false,"can_delete":false,"can_recover":false,"can_see_hidden_post":false,"can_wiki":false,"read":true,"user_title":null,"bookmarked":false,"actions_summary":[],"moderator":false,"admin":false,"staff":false,"user_id":134868,"hidden":false,"trust_level":1,"deleted_at":null,"user_deleted":false,"edit_reason":null,"can_view_edit_history":false,"wiki":false,"post_url":"/t/best-way-to-export-memory/170714/1","reactions":[],"current_user_reaction":null,"reaction_users_count":0,"current_user_used_main_reaction":false,"can_accept_answer":false,"can_unaccept_answer":false,"accepted_answer":false,"topic_accepted_answer":null,"can_vote":false},{"id":485003,"name":"Mohit","username":"mohitjain","avatar_template":"/user_avatar/forum.cursor.com/mohitjain/{size}/100229_2.png","created_at":"2026-09-07T08:08:47.362Z","cooked":"\u003cp\u003eHey \u003ca class=\"mention\" href=\"/u/dannyb\"\u003e@DannyB\u003c/a\u003e thanks for the kind words!\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThere’s no one-click export yet, but you can back everything up by just asking the bots - a bot’s memory lives as plain text files on its own computer that it can zip up and hand back.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003col\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eIn a chat with one bot, paste: “Please make a full backup of your durable state. Make a folder \u003ccode\u003ebackup/\u0026lt;your name\u0026gt;\u003c/code\u003e, copy your complete memory (profile + every memory-log entry, including older months) into memory.md, list your routines (schedule + prompt) in routines.md and your connectors in connectors.md, then zip the folder and send it here as an attachment.” Download the zip when it appears, and repeat for each bot.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eFor shared memory + skills, ask your Chief of Staff: “Copy the shared memory all bots can see into shared-memory.md, zip the skills library folder, and send both here as attachments.”\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eFor other files on the shared computer, tell any bot which folders matter and ask it to zip and send them (attachments cap at 25 MB - for bigger folders ask it to split the zip).\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ol\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eTwo notes: connector logins can’t be exported (the list is just a record), and your SKILL.md-per-topic idea works too - add “also write a SKILL.md for each distinct topic in your memory and include it in the zip” to step 1.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eA proper export/backup is something we’d like to offer - I’ve noted your request (and the pricing feedback) for the team.\u003c/p\u003e","post_number":6,"post_type":1,"posts_count":5,"updated_at":"2026-09-07T08:08:47.362Z","reply_count":1,"reply_to_post_number":null,"quote_count":0,"incoming_link_count":0,"reads":16,"readers_count":15,"score":8.2,"yours":false,"topic_id":170714,"topic_slug":"best-way-to-export-memory","display_username":"Mohit","primary_group_name":"CursorStaff","flair_name":"CursorStaff","flair_url":"https://us1.discourse-cdn.com/cursor1/original/3X/a/d/ad08adc640929ae1e98be69dab1ad0844cee99a0.png","flair_bg_color":"","flair_color":"","flair_group_id":42,"badges_granted":[],"version":1,"can_edit":false,"can_delete":false,"can_recover":false,"can_see_hidden_post":false,"can_wiki":false,"read":true,"user_title":null,"bookmarked":false,"actions_summary":[],"moderator":true,"admin":true,"staff":true,"user_id":103596,"hidden":false,"trust_level":4,"deleted_at":null,"user_deleted":false,"edit_reason":null,"can_view_edit_history":false,"wiki":false,"post_url":"/t/best-way-to-export-memory/170714/6","reactions":[],"current_user_reaction":null,"reaction_users_count":0,"current_user_used_main_reaction":false,"can_accept_answer":false,"can_unaccept_answer":false,"accepted_answer":false,"topic_accepted_answer":null},{"id":485432,"name":"Danny","username":"DannyB","avatar_template":"/user_avatar/forum.cursor.com/dannyb/{size}/119004_2.png","created_at":"2026-09-07T14:03:01.366Z","cooked":"\u003cp\u003eThank you so much for your detailed reply! I will try this soon.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eI’ve seen that you guys have been trying to fix the burn rate of the weekly usage, over the weekend - it seems to be considerably better!! \u003cimg src=\"https://emoji.discourse-cdn.com/fluentui/crossed_fingers/2.png?v=15\" title=\":crossed_fingers:t2:\" class=\"emoji\" alt=\":crossed_fingers:t2:\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\"\u003e I got a reset on the 5th and I’ve used 85% in 2 days, compared to 100% in 1 day. I still haven’t got it running completely autonomously (while I sleep) though, otherwise it would still burn 100% in 1 day.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eFrom my ChatGPT routine that’s monitoring the high burn rate of weekly usage:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cblockquote\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eMeaningful update — 5 September 2026:\u003c/strong\u003e there are \u003cstrong\u003etwo major developments\u003c/strong\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003e1. Grok Bot received another full usage reset for all users.\u003c/strong\u003e The official \u003cstrong\u003e\u003ca class=\"mention\" href=\"/u/bot\"\u003e@bot\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/strong\u003e account announced: “We’ve reset usage limits for all Grok Bot users. Enjoy!” Elon Musk then quote-posted it at \u003cstrong\u003e20:19 UTC / 21:19 BST on 5 September\u003c/strong\u003e, saying \u003cstrong\u003e“Grok \u003ca class=\"mention\" href=\"/u/bot\"\u003e@Bot\u003c/a\u003e usage limits reset.”\u003c/strong\u003e This is another off-cycle reset after the resets on \u003cstrong\u003e26 August\u003c/strong\u003e and \u003cstrong\u003e1 September\u003c/strong\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003e2. More importantly for the rapid-depletion problem, the Grok Bot/Cursor team says it has now shipped substantial token-efficiency improvements.\u003c/strong\u003e Jediah Katz, who describes himself as building the agent at \u003cstrong\u003eCursor and \u003ca class=\"mention\" href=\"/u/bot\"\u003e@bot\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/strong\u003e, says the team spent the previous two weeks improving \u003cstrong\u003erouting, caching, dynamic context usage and overall token efficiency\u003c/strong\u003e. He says Grok Bot usage should now go \u003cstrong\u003eabout 10% further on average, and up to 35% further for certain heavy users\u003c/strong\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eMatt Palmer, who works with Cursor/Grok Bot, summarizes the change even more explicitly: \u003cstrong\u003e“The \u003ca class=\"mention\" href=\"/u/bot\"\u003e@bot\u003c/a\u003e harness is now 10-35% more efficient and usage has been reset for the long weekend.”\u003c/strong\u003e Lauren Tan also says Grok Bot usage “should go further now” and that the team will continue improving efficiency.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThis appears to be the \u003cstrong\u003efirst quantified deployed improvement directly addressing the unusually fast Grok Bot usage depletion\u003c/strong\u003e we’ve been tracking.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003c/blockquote\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eIt linked a few different Twitter posts, but they haven’t pasted.\u003c/p\u003e","post_number":7,"post_type":1,"posts_count":5,"updated_at":"2026-09-07T14:29:37.571Z","reply_count":0,"reply_to_post_number":6,"quote_count":0,"incoming_link_count":2,"reads":15,"readers_count":14,"score":13.0,"yours":false,"topic_id":170714,"topic_slug":"best-way-to-export-memory","display_username":"Danny","primary_group_name":null,"flair_name":null,"flair_url":null,"flair_bg_color":null,"flair_color":null,"flair_group_id":null,"badges_granted":[],"version":5,"can_edit":false,"can_delete":false,"can_recover":false,"can_see_hidden_post":false,"can_wiki":false,"link_counts":[{"url":"https://forum.cursor.com/t/grok-4-5-removed/170631/57","internal":true,"reflection":true,"title":"Grok 4.5 Removed?","clicks":2},{"url":"https://forum.cursor.com/t/share-your-thoughts-on-grok-4-6/168190/109","internal":true,"reflection":true,"title":"Share your Thoughts on Grok 4.6","clicks":0},{"url":"https://forum.cursor.com/t/anyone-used-grokbot-on-the-api-very-high-costs/169551/30","internal":true,"reflection":true,"title":"Anyone used Grokbot on the API - Very high costs?!","clicks":0}],"read":true,"user_title":null,"reply_to_user":{"id":103596,"username":"mohitjain","name":"Mohit","avatar_template":"/user_avatar/forum.cursor.com/mohitjain/{size}/100229_2.png"},"bookmarked":false,"actions_summary":[],"moderator":false,"admin":false,"staff":false,"user_id":134868,"hidden":false,"trust_level":1,"deleted_at":null,"user_deleted":false,"edit_reason":null,"can_view_edit_history":false,"wiki":false,"post_url":"/t/best-way-to-export-memory/170714/7","reactions":[],"current_user_reaction":null,"reaction_users_count":0,"current_user_used_main_reaction":false,"can_accept_answer":false,"can_unaccept_answer":false,"accepted_answer":false,"topic_accepted_answer":null},{"id":488340,"name":"Danny","username":"DannyB","avatar_template":"/user_avatar/forum.cursor.com/dannyb/{size}/119004_2.png","created_at":"2026-09-10T18:32:21.513Z","cooked":"\u003cp\u003eJust to follow up on this, since the team improved the usage, I’m seeing it go twice as far. I probably won’t be trying Hermes. Grok Bot is super awesome!\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eI’m still going to try to build the skills though. Since my original post, I’ve started getting the bots to maintain a directory of skills Markdown files in a Git repo \u003cimg src=\"https://emoji.discourse-cdn.com/fluentui/slight_smile.png?v=15\" title=\":slight_smile:\" class=\"emoji\" alt=\":slight_smile:\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\"\u003e And one of my skills is \u003ccode\u003e/update\u003c/code\u003e which grabs the latest skills from the Git repo and installs them in Grok Bot \u003cimg src=\"https://emoji.discourse-cdn.com/fluentui/smiley.png?v=15\" title=\":smiley:\" class=\"emoji\" alt=\":smiley:\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\"\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eI haven’t tried to export memory yet, but I do think it would great to codify a lot of my memories in to skills. It will no doubt be a fairly involved task to do, but I might try it eventually lol.\u003c/p\u003e","post_number":8,"post_type":1,"posts_count":5,"updated_at":"2026-09-10T18:35:11.006Z","reply_count":0,"reply_to_post_number":null,"quote_count":0,"incoming_link_count":0,"reads":3,"readers_count":2,"score":0.6,"yours":false,"topic_id":170714,"topic_slug":"best-way-to-export-memory","display_username":"Danny","primary_group_name":null,"flair_name":null,"flair_url":null,"flair_bg_color":null,"flair_color":null,"flair_group_id":null,"badges_granted":[],"version":3,"can_edit":false,"can_delete":false,"can_recover":false,"can_see_hidden_post":false,"can_wiki":false,"read":true,"user_title":null,"bookmarked":false,"actions_summary":[],"moderator":false,"admin":false,"staff":false,"user_id":134868,"hidden":false,"trust_level":1,"deleted_at":null,"user_deleted":false,"edit_reason":null,"can_view_edit_history":false,"wiki":false,"post_url":"/t/best-way-to-export-memory/170714/8","reactions":[],"current_user_reaction":null,"reaction_users_count":0,"current_user_used_main_reaction":false,"can_accept_answer":false,"can_unaccept_answer":false,"accepted_answer":false,"topic_accepted_answer":null},{"id":488441,"name":"Edward Izgorodin","username":"izgorodin","avatar_template":"/user_avatar/forum.cursor.com/izgorodin/{size}/117016_2.png","created_at":"2026-09-10T22:18:17.476Z","cooked":"\u003cp\u003eI’d keep the backup and the skill library separate. Skills are reusable behavior; memory is user or task state with provenance, timestamps, scope, and often an expiry, so converting it wholesale into SKILL.md can freeze stale facts into instructions. Export the raw memory plus a manifest, test a clean restore, and promote only stable, reviewed procedures into skills.\u003c/p\u003e","post_number":10,"post_type":1,"posts_count":5,"updated_at":"2026-09-10T22:18:17.476Z","reply_count":0,"reply_to_post_number":null,"quote_count":0,"incoming_link_count":0,"reads":1,"readers_count":0,"score":0.2,"yours":false,"topic_id":170714,"topic_slug":"best-way-to-export-memory","display_username":"Edward Izgorodin","primary_group_name":null,"flair_name":null,"flair_url":null,"flair_bg_color":null,"flair_color":null,"flair_group_id":null,"badges_granted":[],"version":1,"can_edit":false,"can_delete":false,"can_recover":false,"can_see_hidden_post":false,"can_wiki":false,"read":true,"user_title":"","bookmarked":false,"actions_summary":[],"moderator":false,"admin":false,"staff":false,"user_id":131853,"hidden":false,"trust_level":1,"deleted_at":null,"user_deleted":false,"edit_reason":null,"can_view_edit_history":false,"wiki":false,"post_url":"/t/best-way-to-export-memory/170714/10","reactions":[],"current_user_reaction":null,"reaction_users_count":0,"current_user_used_main_reaction":false,"can_accept_answer":false,"can_unaccept_answer":false,"accepted_answer":false,"topic_accepted_answer":null}],"stream":[484170,485003,485432,488340,488441]},"timeline_lookup":[[1,5],[2,4],[3,3],[4,0]],"suggested_topics":[],"tags":[{"id":416,"name":"grok-bot","slug":"grok-bot"},{"id":299,"name":"skills","slug":"skills"}],"tags_descriptions":{},"fancy_title":"Best way to export memory","id":170714,"t